  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "$\\int 8\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u20612\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\,\u21d2\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20614x & =\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20614x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\operatorname{sin}\u20614x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x)+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
